{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>לרצנכם תזבחהו.</b> Put your will into it — do not be stingy with what you bring before HaKadosh Baruch Hu, for there are people who do not offer from the heart, but only because they see other people, their fellows, doing so, and they are ashamed if they do not do likewise. Another interpretation: do a thing that will be favorable (לרצון) for you — how so? If on the day of your offering (זבחכם) it is eaten, and on the next day." "<b>תזבחהו.</b> One does not slaughter two heads at once."], :book :leviticus, :voice :chizkuni, :lang :en, :chapter 19, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T15:13:25.783972496Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}